    implicit_self_field_read_unresolved_in_plain_fn_method_2026-09-03, 990, "2026-11-09 revalidation (work/p3-subj2-native-20261109): lane split. Pure-Simple HIR lane FIXED: the doc 12-line repro (class Box, plain fn code() reading `kind` bare) lowers with zero errors via HirLowering at release/1.0.0 HEAD (new spec test/01_unit/compiler/hir/implicit_self_field_read_plain_fn_spec.spl 1/1 PASS on seed interpreter). Rust seed lane still RED: `seed run` on the same repro dies with GlobalLoad: unresolved identifier 'kind' (JIT) then semantic: variable `kind` not found (interpreter fallback). Not closed; remaining failure lives in compiler_rust codegen/semantic lanes, outside the pure-Simple fix scope."
    implicit_self_field_read_unresolved_in_plain_fn_method_2026-09-03, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: reproduced on a baseline scratch build of HEAD (GlobalLoad: unresolved identifier kind -> JIT demotion -> interpreter semantic: variable kind not found, exit 1). Root cause (two layers): (1) the seed parser marked a class-body fn with no explicit self/me param as is_static (parser/src/types_def/mod.rs) so HIR never put a receiver in scope unless the body literally spells self (function.rs:1398 - TAKEN), while the pure-Simple frontend synthesizes self for every non-constructor class-body method; (2) the bare name lowered to an unresolved Global typed ANY whose GlobalLoad died in codegen - the read had to be re-typed to the field's declared type like an explicit self.kind. Fix (all outside TAKEN sets): types_def/mod.rs plain-fn class methods now get a synthesized immutable self param (constructor-named factories new/create/default/from_* stay static, preserving the FlatPoolReader calling-convention fix); trait_impl_parsing.rs is_constructor_name now pub(crate); NEW mir/lower/receiver_field_rewrite.rs - before per-function analysis in lower_function, method bodies are probed and (only when a candidate exists, function cloned) unresolved Global(name) reads matching a receiver field and no known symbol are rewritten to concretely typed self.<field> HirExprs; lambda bodies and assignment targets excluded; lowering_expr_ident.rs residual net for contract clauses; mod.rs registers the module. Verification on the patched scratch: doc repro prints code=4 exit 0; itf_config_spec 32/32 before (via the self.kind workaround) AND after - no regression; new spec test/01_unit/language/implicit_self_field_read_plain_fn_jit_spec.spl (SIMPLE_BINARY convention, JIT child runs) RED 3/4 on baseline to GREEN 4/4 patched (doc repro, else-branch, me-method parity, unknown-name fail-closed guard); extra probes (two-field sums, reads through vals, naked returns, f64 arithmetic, bool conditions) all correct; canaries devhub_errors 14/14, cmd_jira 12/12, jit_list_comprehension 2/2, engine_divergence_mutation_class 2/2, for_loop_struct_element_by_value 3/3, run_semantic_error_exit_code 4/4 green on both. Re-verification guide: doc/07_guide/compiler/seed_implicit_self_field_read_reverification.md. Residuals: the tree-walk interpreter's literal-resolution path for bare reads still needs its own patch (design: in interpreter/expr/literals.rs:522 after scope-miss, resolve to a receiver field load - the parser half of this fix already gives it the self param; itf_config passes through the interpreter today, owning lane should confirm); struct bodies have the identical latent static-marking shape (same one-hunk fix applies if desired - kept class-scoped); bare reads in Calc/InlineAsm/ProofHint positions and lambda bodies keep fail-closed by design. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/language/implicit_self_field_read_plain_fn_jit_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/app/devhub/itf_config_spec.spl"
    implicit_self_field_read_unresolved_in_plain_fn_method_2026-09-03, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: reproduced on a baseline scratch build of HEAD (GlobalLoad unresolved identifier kind, exit 1). Root cause: the seed parser marked class-body fn with no explicit self/me as is_static so HIR never scoped a receiver (function.rs:1398 TAKEN), while pure-Simple synthesizes self for every non-constructor method; the bare name lowered to an unresolved ANY Global. Fix (all outside TAKEN): parser types_def/mod.rs synthesizes an immutable self param (constructor-named factories new/create/default/from_* stay static); trait_impl_parsing is_constructor_name pub(crate); NEW mir/lower/receiver_field_rewrite.rs rewrites unresolved Global(name) reads matching a receiver field to concretely typed self.<field> (lambda bodies + assignment targets excluded); lowering_expr_ident.rs residual net. Verification on the patched scratch: doc repro code=4 exit 0; itf_config_spec 32/32 before (self.kind workaround) AND after; spec implicit_self_field_read_plain_fn_jit RED 3/4 to GREEN 4/4; canaries devhub_errors 14/14, cmd_jira 12/12, jit_list_comprehension 2/2, engine_divergence_mutation_class 2/2, for_loop_struct_element_by_value 3/3, run_semantic_error_exit_code 4/4. Re-verification guide: doc/07_guide/compiler/seed_implicit_self_field_read_reverification.md. Residuals: the tree-walk interpreter's literal-resolution path for bare reads still needs its own patch (design documented; itf_config passes through the interpreter today); struct bodies have the identical latent shape (kept class-scoped); Calc/InlineAsm/ProofHint positions keep fail-closed by design. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/language/implicit_self_field_read_plain_fn_jit_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/app/devhub/itf_config_spec.spl"

